1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,070
Listen to a short talk on history.

2
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:06,280
OK. Since we've been talking about mechanics and then we still have a few minutes.

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:09,040
Let me tell you a little about the ancient Greeks

4
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:11,040
and what they thought about mechanics.

5
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:14,658
They came up with a system that for them seem to describe

6
00:00:14,658 --> 00:00:17,070
and explain the different motions of different materials.

7
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:21,215
More than 2000 years ago, Aristotle, the ancient Greek philosopher,

8
00:00:21,215 --> 00:00:25,680
assumed that all the matter on earth were made up of four prime substances

9
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:29,090
earth, water, air and fire.

10
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:31,432
Under this system, earth is the densest,

11
00:00:31,432 --> 00:00:37,120
water is the next, air is less dense than water, and fire is least dense of all.

12
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:40,028
The heaviest object was made of earth and water,

13
00:00:40,028 --> 00:00:43,260
and lighter object contains significant amounts of fire or air.

14
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:48,100
So when Aristotle observed that different types of matter had different characteristics.

15
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:54,270
He assumed this was because the different types of matter were composed of different amounts of four primary substances.

16
00:00:54,270 --> 00:01:01,200
And Aristotle believes that the motions of objects could also be explained by the basic natures of four primary substances.

17
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:05,230
Hum, for example, there was a basic motion of up or down.

18
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:10,190
Aristotle noticed that when he released most objects, they would drop downwards.

19
00:01:10,190 --> 00:01:14,000
But he also knew that something would rise upwards, like smoke.

20
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,100
Aristotle considered an object downward or upward motion to be the result of dominant nature of the object.

21
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:24,361
So according to Aristotle, matter like rock were primarily composed of earth, therefore,

22
00:01:24,361 --> 00:01:28,220
they naturally want to move toward the center of the earth

23
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:30,260
because this was all thing earthly rested.

24
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:33,260
But fire had a different resting place, the sky.

25
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:36,740
So smoke would naturally rise when it was released

26
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:40,050
because it was driving toward its natural resting place.
